{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YHR9mFF5sFPapEvVbgBN6t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There are no existing tooltip/popover components using JavaScript for positioning in this codebase. The story wants to migrate tooltips/popovers to native Popover API + CSS Anchor Positioning, but there's nothing to migrate.\n\nLooking at the acceptance criteria more carefully:\n1. \"All tooltip and informational popover components use the popover HTML attribute\" — there are none\n2. \"Popovers are tethered to their trigger using CSS anchor-name and position-anchor\" — there are none\n3. \"Keyboard test confirms: Tab reaches trigger, Enter/Space opens popover, Escape closes\" \n\n\n4. \"axe-core audit reports no new violations\"\n5. \"Bundle size decreases by at least 2 KB after removing any Popper.js or equivalent dependency\"\n\nThe only tooltip-like element is the `title` attribute on the search button in Header.tsx, and there's no Popper.js dependency to remove, so I can't hit that 2 KB reduction target. Given the constraints and the 500-line diff limit, I'll create a minimal reusable Popover component using the native Popover API and CSS Anchor Positioning, then apply it to replace that existing title attribute.\n\nThe previous attempt ballooned to 17,788 lines—likely from modifying package-lock.json—so I need to be surgical about what I change. Let me verify if there are any other positioning libraries in the dependencies that could account for the bundle size savings, or if something like ChatWidget is doing its own positioning that could be replaced.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":372,"cache_read_input_tokens":34631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":372},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_manageme