{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01N9E48XBLekZ4scvF5i2P9T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so there's:\n- No Popper.js or @floating-ui or any JS tooltip/positioning library in dependencies\n- No `getBoundingClientRect`-based positioning for tooltips\n- No existing tooltip/popover components at all\n- The only tooltip-like thing is `title=\"Search (Ctrl+K)\"` in Header.tsx\n\nThis codebase doesn't actually have JavaScript tooltip positioning to replace. The story seems to be forward-looking — creating new tooltip/popover components using native APIs.\n\nGiven the constraints (500-line diff limit, no existing libraries to remove), the right approach is:\n\n\n1. Create a minimal `InfoPopover` component using native Popover API + CSS Anchor Positioning\n2. Add minimal CSS for anchor positioning with `@supports` fallback\n3. Apply it to 1-2 existing places where `title` attributes or info text could benefit from popovers (e.g., Header search button, maybe an amenity info)\n4. The \"bundle size decrease\" criterion can't be met since there's no library to remove — but I can note this in the implementation\n\nActually, re-reading the acceptance criteria more carefully: the bundle size requirement assumes there's a Popper.js or equivalent dependency to remove, but this codebase doesn't have one, so that criterion isn't applicable here.\n\nFor a minimal implementation that satisfies the story, I'd create a reusable `InfoPopover` component using the native popover attribute and CSS anchor positioning, add the necessary CSS with fallbacks, then apply it surgically to the Header search button and maybe one or two other places like amenities or booking info — keeping the total diff well under 500 lines.\n\nNow I'm checking what existing components might already have popover-like behavior with JS-based show/hide mechanics, like the ChatWidget or SearchDialog, to see if there's something I can build on rather than create from scratch. But realistically, the fastest path is to implement a lightweight native popover solution and hunt for `title` attributes that could be converted to proper tooltip popovers across a few key components.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2881,"cache_read_input_tokens":35003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2881},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01df7ad1-8a9a-45d7-80b2-f9b95ad91d60","uuid":"2555f34b-0b1d-40a6-859b-e155d7b020d6"}
